2. **"Packs flat. Holds a full plate lunch. Fits your backpack."**
   Leads on portability and capacity — the "it actually fits in your bag" objection — rather than freshness or waste.

The original headline promises food quality (crisp rice); these two promise saving money and fitting your gear. Pick based on which objection you think stops students from buying.
